  "description": "Two standalone machines: Buff (Windows) — Gym Management → Chisel tunnel → CloudMe BOF → Administrator. Hawk (Linux) — FTP anon → OpenSSL brute → Drupal creds → H2 database RCE → root.",
  "introduction": "This scenario teaches tunneling to reach internal services and buffer overflow exploitation. Chisel tunnels are common in OSCP for accessing localhost-only services.",
  "mental_model": "When a service runs only on localhost, tunnel it: Chisel reverse exposes 127.0.0.1:port to your Kali. Buffer overflows often give full compromise.",
  "key_principles": [
    "Chisel reverse tunnel exposes internal ports to Kali",
    "CloudMe BOF on 8888 requires tunnel from foothold",
    "FTP anonymous often has encrypted credential files",
    "OpenSSL enc -d brute decrypts with rockyou",
    "H2 database console often has RCE as root"
  ],

